{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1780696277156,"sessionID":"ses_1663b4e44ffe8jSrEsklnuFx6V","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"toolu_vrtx_01SM9n8a7bYpfMFEo3aGbuDd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/reading-advantage-monorepo/measure/tracks/ai_adapter_package_20260603/plan.md"},"output":"<path>/home/daniel-bo/Desktop/reading-advantage-monorepo/measure/tracks/ai_adapter_package_20260603/plan.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Plan: Shared `packages/ai` + `lib/ai/` Refactor\n2: \n3: > TDD-first. Mock provider is implemented first; OpenAI and Google providers are tested against the mock's interface contract.\n4: \n5: ## Phase 0: Setup\n6: \n7: - [ ] Task: Confirm `packages/` directory has no `ai/` package today. Initialize `packages/ai/` with `package.json`, `tsconfig.json` (extending monorepo shared config), and `src/index.ts` barrel.\n8: - [ ] Task: Add `@node-rs/argon2` and `ai` / `@ai-sdk/openai` / `@ai-sdk/google` to `packages/ai/package.json` `dependencies`. Pin versions per AGENTS.md §Version Policy.\n9: - [ ] Task: Add to monorepo root `pnpm-workspace.yaml` if not already.\n10: - [ ] Task: Pull `apps/science-advantage`; confirm baseline tests pass.\n11: \n12: ## Phase 1: `AIClient` Interface\n13: \n14: - [ ] Task: Create `packages/ai/src/types.ts` with the `AIClient` interface, `GenerateObjectInput`, `GenerateImageInput`, `GenerateTextInput` (FR-1).\n15: - [ ] Task: Create `packages/ai/src/errors.ts` with `AIClientError`, `ProviderNotConfiguredError`, `SchemaValidationError`.\n16: - [ ] Task: Export from `packages/ai/src/index.ts` barrel.\n17: \n18: ## Phase 2: Mock Provider\n19: \n20: - [ ] Task: Create `packages/ai/src/providers/mock.ts` implementing `AIClient`.\n21: - [ ] Task: Mock takes a `responses: { generateObject?: ..., generateImage?: ..., generateText?: ... }` config in the constructor. If a response is configured, return it; otherwise throw `ProviderNotConfiguredError`.\n22: - [ ] Task: Write failing tests:\n23:   - `mock.generateObject({ schema, prompt: 'test' })` with a configured response returns the configured object.\n24:   - `mock.generateImage({ prompt: 'test' })` with a configured response returns a Buffer.\n25:   - `mock.generateText({ prompt: 'test' })` with no configured response throws.\n26:   - `mock.generateObject` validates the response against the schema; invalid response throws `SchemaValidationError`.\n27: - [ ] Task: Implement. Confirm tests pass.\n28: - [ ] Task: Add snapshot test: feed a prompt, capture the response, snapshot for regression.\n29: \n30: ## Phase 3: OpenAI Provider\n31: \n32: - [ ] Task: Create `packages/ai/src/providers/openai.ts` implementing `AIClient` using `@ai-sdk/openai`.\n33: - [ ] Task: Constructor takes `{ apiKey, model?, organization? }`. **No `process.env` reads** — the API key is passed explicitly.\n34: - [ ] Task: `generateObject` uses Vercel AI SDK `generateObject` with the configured client.\n35: - [ ] Task: Write failing tests with the mock as the \"openai\" provider's underlying model (avoid real network): assert the OpenAI provider delegates to `generateObject` with the right schema and prompt.\n36: - [ ] Task: Add a single integration test that hits the real OpenAI API (gated by `OPENAI_API_KEY` env in CI). Confirm response shape.\n37: - [ ] Task: Confirm tests pass.\n38: \n39: ## Phase 4: Google Provider\n40: \n41: - [ ] Task: Create `packages/ai/src/providers/google.ts` implementing `AIClient` using `@ai-sdk/google`.\n42: - [ ] Task: Same pattern as OpenAI provider; constructor takes `{ apiKey, model? }`.\n43: - [ ] Task: Write failing tests with the mock as the underlying model.\n44: - [ ] Task: Add a single integration test gated by `GEMINI_API_KEY` env.\n45: - [ ] Task: Confirm.\n46: \n47: ## Phase 5: Provider Selector\n48: \n49: - [ ] Task: Create `packages/ai/src/client.ts` with `createAIClient(config: AIConfig)` and `getAIClient()` lazy singleton.\n50: - [ ] Task: `AIConfig` Zod schema: `{ provider: z.enum(['openai', 'google', 'mock']).default('openai'), apiKey: z.string().optional(), model: z.string().optional(), organization: z.string().optional() }`.\n51: - [ ] Task: `getAIClient()` reads `AI_PROVIDER`, `OPENAI_API_KEY`, `GEMINI_API_KEY`, `AI_RECOMMENDER_MODEL` from `process.env` (via the validated `env` from Track 7, when available) and constructs the right provider.\n52: - [ ] Task: Write failing tests:\n53:   - `getAIClient()` with `AI_PROVIDER='mock'` returns the mock provider.\n54:   - `getAIClient()` with `AI_PROVIDER='openai'` + `OPENAI_API_KEY='test-key'` returns the OpenAI provider.\n55:   - `getAIClient()` with no env vars + `NODE_ENV='production'` throws `ProviderNotConfiguredError`.\n56:   - `getAIClient()` with no env vars + `NODE_ENV='test'` returns the mock provider.\n57: - [ ] Task: Confirm.\n58: \n59: ## Phase 6: Refactor `lib/ai/recommendation-service.ts`\n60: \n61: - [ ] Task: Write a failing test for the new `RecommendationService` class (constructor takes `AIClient`; `getRecommendation(input)` calls `client.generateObject(...)`).\n62: - [ ] Task: Replace the direct `generateObject` import with `getAIClient().generateObject(...)`.\n63: - [ ] Task: Refactor the existing `generateRecommendation(input)` exported function into a thin wrapper that calls the service.\n64: - [ ] Task: Update the call site `app/api/ai/recommendations/route.ts:21` to use the new wrapper (or the service directly).\n65: - [ ] Task: Run `pnpm turbo run test --filter=science-advantage`; the existing tests should still pass (the wrapper preserves the public API).\n66: \n67: ## Phase 7: Refactor `lib/ai/image-generator.ts`\n68: \n69: - [ ] Task: Write a failing test for the new `ImageGenerator` class (constructor takes `AIClient`; `generateDiagram(input)` calls `client.generateImage(...)`).\n70: - [ ] Task: **Remove the `process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY` / `process.env.GOOGLE_API_KEY` mutation** in `ensureApiKey()`. The API key is passed via the `AIClient` constructor (set in Phase 5 by `getAIClient()`).\n71: - [ ] Task: Refactor the existing `generateLessonDiagram(input)` exported function into a thin wrapper.\n72: - [ ] Task: Update call sites in `components/features/lesson/blocks/image-block.tsx` etc.\n73: - [ ] Task: Run `pnpm turbo run test --filter=science-advantage`; confirm.\n74: \n75: ## Phase 8: Remove Direct Provider SDK Deps\n76: \n77: - [ ] Task: Remove `ai`, `@ai-sdk/openai`, `@ai-sdk/google` from `apps/science-advantage/package.json` `dependencies`.\n78: - [ ] Task: Add `@reading-advantage/ai` to `dependencies` (workspace:*).\n79: - [ ] Task: `pnpm install` from monorepo root; verify no errors.\n80: - [ ] Task: Grep gate: `rg \"from ['\\\"]@?ai['\\\"]|from ['\\\"]@ai-sdk\" apps/science-advantage/` returns 0 hits.\n81: - [ ] Task: Grep gate: `rg \"process\\.env\\.(OPENAI_API_KEY|GOOGLE_API_KEY|GEMINI_API_KEY)\" apps/science-advantage/lib/ai/` returns 0 hits.\n82: \n83: ## Phase 9: Update Docs\n84: \n85: - [ ] Task: Update `apps/science-advantage/docs/specs/ai-structured-data-generation/spec.md:79-86` to reference `@reading-advantage/ai` interface.\n86: - [ ] Task: Update `apps/science-advantage/docs/ai-image-generation.md:9` similarly.\n87: - [ ] Task: Write `packages/ai/README.md` with provider config examples.\n88: \n89: ## Phase 10: Closeout\n90: \n91: - [ ] Task: Update `measure/tech-debt.md` row `audit_20260603_housekeeping_batch` to mark F-101, F-202 `Resolved`.\n92: - [ ] Task: Add a lessons-learned entry: \"The mock provider with snapshot tests is the unit-test pattern; the real provider is integration-tested only with API keys present in env.\"\n93: - [ ] Task: Move track to `measure/archive/ai_adapter_package_20260603/` and update `measure/tracks.md`.\n\n(End of file - total 93 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Plan: Shared `packages/ai` + `lib/ai/` Refactor\n\n> TDD-first. Mock provider is implemented first; OpenAI and Google providers are tested against the mock's interface contract.\n\n#